      "attestations": [
        {
          "text": "P'ÊNG Sun-i 彭孫貽 (T. 仲謀, 羿仁, H. 茗齋, 管葛山人, 管山人), July 7, 1615–1673, historian and poet, was a native of Hai-yen, Chekiang. His father, P'êng Ch'i-shêng 彭期生 (T. 孝弱, 觀民, H. 弱水道人), Jan. 20, 1584–1646), was a chin-shih of 1616, who died a martyr to the Ming cause after failing to defend the city of Kanchow, Kiangsi, against the Ch'ing armies.",
